From: Nicolas Michaut <nicolas@yumilab.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: dwmac-sun8i: reset the EMAC at probe, not at open
Date: 2026-10-12

Undo Armbian's patches.armbian/drv-net-stmmac-dwmac-sun8i-reset-emac-on-open.patch
(armbian/build #10492, in the sunxi-6.18 series since 2026-09-07) for this
board: it brings the driver back to mainline.

That patch moves the MAC soft reset into sun8i_dwmac_dma_reset(), which
stmmac calls at every ndo_open. The soft reset only completes while the
PHY drives the receive clock. When the H3 internal PHY runs on the Generic
PHY driver and no cable is plugged in, it does not complete within the
100 ms the driver waits:

  dwmac-sun8i 1c30000.ethernet eth0: Failed to reset the dma
  dwmac-sun8i 1c30000.ethernet eth0: stmmac_hw_setup: DMA engine initialization failed
  dwmac-sun8i 1c30000.ethernet eth0: __stmmac_open: Hw setup failed

The open fails, eth0 stays down, and since a down interface does not watch
its link, a cable plugged in afterwards is never seen: no Ethernet until
the next boot with the cable in, or a manual "ip link set eth0 up".

A freshly flashed image is exactly in that situation: its initramfs holds
no PHY driver at all (checked in the published 2026-10-11-1408 image: 241
modules, none from drivers/net/phy), phylib only asks for the driver
module when it creates the PHY, 2 s into the boot, so ac200-phy cannot be
loaded and the PHY falls back to "Generic PHY". Once an initramfs has been
regenerated on the board (646 modules, ac200-phy included) the PHY gets
"Allwinner AC200 EPHY" instead and the reset passes, which is why the
fault seems to come and go.

Measured on a SmartPi One, no cable, 6.18.56 (2026-10-12):
  - Armbian's patch, Generic PHY:   7 boots, 7 failures (4 on the fresh
    image, 3 with ac200_phy blacklisted to pin the driver)
  - Armbian's patch, AC200 EPHY:    9 boots with a regenerated initramfs,
    0 failure
  - this patch, Generic PHY:        4 boots, 0 failure
  - this patch, AC200 EPHY:         2 boots, 0 failure

Armbian's patch fixes Ethernet lost after a warm reboot on H616/H618
boards with an external PHY. The SmartPi One only has the internal PHY,
which the driver powers and resets itself at probe, so that case does
not apply here.

If Armbian drops or reworks its patch, this one stops applying and the
build says so: delete this file then.

Signed-off-by: Nicolas Michaut <nicolas@yumilab.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c | 49 ++++------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
@@ -272,34 +272,8 @@
 /* sun8i_dwmac_dma_reset() - reset the EMAC
  * Called from stmmac via stmmac_dma_ops->reset
  */
-static int sun8i_dwmac_soft_reset(void __iomem *ioaddr)
-{
-	u32 v;
-
-	v = readl(ioaddr + EMAC_BASIC_CTL1);
-	writel(v | 0x01, ioaddr + EMAC_BASIC_CTL1);
-
-	/* The timeout was previoulsy set to 10ms, but some board (OrangePI0)
-	 * need more if no cable plugged. 100ms seems OK
-	 */
-	return readl_poll_timeout(ioaddr + EMAC_BASIC_CTL1, v,
-				  !(v & 0x01), 100, 100000);
-}
-
 static int sun8i_dwmac_dma_reset(void __iomem *ioaddr)
 {
-	int err;
-
-	/* The MAC soft reset only completes once the PHY is driving the RX
-	 * clock. Doing it here rather than at probe means phylib has already
-	 * attached and resumed the PHY, so the clock is running by
-	 * construction -- including after a warm reboot that left the PHY
-	 * powered down.
-	 */
-	err = sun8i_dwmac_soft_reset(ioaddr);
-	if (err)
-		return err;
-
 	writel(0, ioaddr + EMAC_RX_CTL1);
 	writel(0, ioaddr + EMAC_TX_CTL1);
 	writel(0, ioaddr + EMAC_RX_FRM_FLT);
@@ -766,12 +740,23 @@
 
 static int sun8i_dwmac_reset(struct stmmac_priv *priv)
 {
-	int err = sun8i_dwmac_soft_reset(priv->ioaddr);
+	u32 v;
+	int err;
 
-	if (err)
-		dev_err(priv->device, "EMAC reset timeout\n");
+	v = readl(priv->ioaddr + EMAC_BASIC_CTL1);
+	writel(v | 0x01, priv->ioaddr + EMAC_BASIC_CTL1);
 
-	return err;
+	/* The timeout was previoulsy set to 10ms, but some board (OrangePI0)
+	 * need more if no cable plugged. 100ms seems OK
+	 */
+	err = readl_poll_timeout(priv->ioaddr + EMAC_BASIC_CTL1, v,
+				 !(v & 0x01), 100, 100000);
+
+	if (err) {
+		dev_err(priv->device, "EMAC reset timeout\n");
+		return err;
+	}
+	return 0;
 }
 
 /* Search in mdio-mux node for internal PHY node and get its clk/reset */
@@ -1240,6 +1225,10 @@
 			dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Failed to register mux\n");
 			goto dwmac_mux;
 		}
+	} else {
+		ret = sun8i_dwmac_reset(priv);
+		if (ret)
+			goto dwmac_remove;
 	}
 
 	pm_runtime_put(&pdev->dev);
